# NewBe Licensing

Copyright (c) 2026 NewBe contributors.

NewBe uses a split license so its software and original visual artwork can be reused under terms appropriate to each kind of work.

## MIT License

The following are licensed under the MIT License in [LICENSES/MIT.txt](LICENSES/MIT.txt):

- source code and executable scripts;
- GNOME Shell extension code and schemas;
- GTK and GNOME Shell CSS;
- build, installation, audit, workflow, configuration, and documentation files;
- generated theme files derived from the MIT-licensed CSS.

This includes `.github/`, `extension/`, `gnome-shell/`, `gtk-3.0/`, `gtk-4.0/`, `scripts/`, `themes/`, and repository text/configuration files unless stated otherwise.

## Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International

The following original visual works are licensed under CC BY-SA 4.0 in [LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt](LICENSES/CC-BY-SA-4.0.txt):

- `assets/wallpapers/`;
- `cursors/` and compiled cursor artwork in `icons/NewBe/cursors/`;
- icon artwork in `icons/NewBe/`;
- preview artwork and live desktop screenshots in `docs/images/` and
  `docs/screenshots/`.

Generated or resized versions remain under the same license as their source artwork.

Application names, product names, and trademarks depicted or referenced by compatibility icons remain the property of their respective owners. The licenses above do not grant trademark rights.
